                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15772979" author="dkarachentsev" created="Fri, 23 Dec 2016 14:14:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Valentin,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m not sure that throwing exception is a good idea, may be it will be enough to show meaningful warnings?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15773467" author="vkulichenko" created="Fri, 23 Dec 2016 18:49:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Dmitry, why don&apos;t you like an exception? I can&apos;t imagine a use case when the described situation can be valid.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15777772" author="dkarachentsev" created="Mon, 26 Dec 2016 07:25:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m just worrying if node unable to connect because another app is listening on that port, and may be it is better not to fail immediately, but go on with next address from list.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In case that you suggested, discovery will fail fast with recommendation to check configuration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But anyway, you&apos;re right and this is also not valid case.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15778747" author="vkulichenko" created="Mon, 26 Dec 2016 18:09:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fail fast is correct behavior here, I think.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15780260" author="dkarachentsev" created="Tue, 27 Dec 2016 12:00:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1382&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PR#1382&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15826007" author="sboikov" created="Tue, 17 Jan 2017 13:05:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reviewed, looks ok.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15829507" author="dkarachentsev" created="Thu, 19 Jan 2017 08:20:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;May fail on constant node restarting. Should be more durable.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15871514" author="sboikov" created="Fri, 17 Feb 2017 09:26:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks good, just in case lt&apos;s set sslConnectAttempts to 3.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
